  "appliesTo": "Warwickshire County Council sets term and holiday dates for all community and voluntary controlled schools.",
  "academyNote": "Academies, foundation, and aided schools set their own dates, and we work with them to keep dates as similar as possible. Academies and free schools set their own training days.",
  "localFacts": [
    {
      "fact": "Warwickshire sets two of the five teacher training days itself and leaves three to schools: 1 September 2026 and 4 January 2027 in 2026-27, 1 September 2027 and 5 January 2028 in 2027-28.",
      "source": "https://www.warwickshire.gov.uk/schoolholidaydates"
    },
    {
      "fact": "The council sets its dates on stated parameters: 195 school days, holidays in full weeks where possible, a three-weekend break at Christmas and Easter, a summer holiday close to six weeks and a pattern close to neighbouring councils.",
      "source": "https://www.warwickshire.gov.uk/schoolholidaydates"
    },
    {
      "fact": "Dates are usually published 18 months before the academic year starts; dates for 2025-26 were published by March 2024.",
      "source": "https://www.warwickshire.gov.uk/schoolholidaydates"
    },
    {
      "fact": "There is one secondary induction day for all Warwickshire schools: Wednesday 8 July 2026, Wednesday 7 July 2027 and Wednesday 5 July 2028.",
      "source": "https://www.warwickshire.gov.uk/schoolholidaydates"
    },
    {
      "fact": "Unlike most West Midlands neighbours, Warwickshire starts 2027-28 on Wednesday 1 September 2027 and returns after Christmas on Wednesday 5 January 2028, both teacher training days.",
      "source": "https://www.warwickshire.gov.uk/schoolholidaydates"
    },
    {
      "fact": "The council publishes a list of closed schools when schools tell it, for example during severe weather.",
      "source": "https://www.warwickshire.gov.uk/schoolholidaydates"
    }
  ],
